{"type":"message","id":"c0c570bf","parentId":"7ec3efaf","timestamp":"2026-05-19T00:16:55.464Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101 errors. The error code 1101 from Cloudflare Workers means \"JavaScript error thrown\". This might be an issue with how the worker handles the request.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe there's an issue with the Content-Type header format. Let me also try with --data-raw instead of -d.\n\nOr maybe the issue is that the worker can't handle the JSON being sent. Let me check if there's something wrong with the JSON format itself.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the original request. The user wants me to:\n1. GET /history (worked with X-API-Key)\n2. If new discussions found, read and respond\n3. POST /send to respond\n\n\n4. But the POST endpoint is throwing a 1101 error while GET works fine with X-API-Key, so the issue might be with how the request body is being processed. Let me try sending the data as a query parameter instead, or check if there's something specific about the worker code that's failing when handling POST requests.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-42a2ac50-52ef-45c5-a720-d4ae8ff180a6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  --data-raw '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test\"}' \\\n  \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" -v 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":277,"output":308,"cacheRead":19408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19993,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779149809201,"responseId":"chatcmpl-43e5a448-333f-45c0-9b07-0e43a4376f67"}}
