{"type":"message","id":"aa29fc28","parentId":"d872669d","timestamp":"2026-05-19T00:17:15.277Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101. The POST /send endpoint seems to be broken or has some specific requirements. Let me check the GET /send endpoint - maybe it works differently.\n\nActually, I recall the user gave me the API_KEY but maybe I should double check the exact auth format. The GET /history worked with X-API-Key. The POST /send fails with 1101. This is a Cloudflare Workers error. 1101 is \"Worker threw exception\" - a JavaScript runtime error.\n\nThis might be an issue with the echo-agent platform code - perhaps the /send endpoint has a bug or requires additional fields. Since I can't fix the server-side issue, I should report this back to the user.\n\nBut wait - maybe there's a workaround. \n\nThe error 1101 suggests the worker itself is crashing on the POST request, which could mean the endpoint is expecting fields I'm not providing or there's a genuine code issue on the server side. I should report this to the user since the /send endpoint appears to be non-functional.\n\nNow I'm compiling the heartbeat status report showing the system is running normally across both threads with no new human discussions that need responses, though the messaging endpoint is throwing a Worker exception that needs attention.\n\nLet me check if I can work around the POST issue by using query parameters instead, or maybe the endpoint expects a different content-type altogether.\n\nActually, I should step back—GET worked fine with X-API-Key but POST is throwing a 1101 error, which suggests the Cloudflare Worker itself is crashing when it tries to process the request body. This is a server-side issue I can't fix from here. Let me document what I've found for the user.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2596e795-5b49-4850-90be-051e1cf3e6eb","name":"exec","arguments"